# AI Career OS
## State Management & Application Logic Specification v1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines how application state is managed throughout AI Career OS.

Every page, component, hook, API, and AI-generated feature must follow these rules.

The objective is to create a predictable, scalable, maintainable application where data has a single source of truth and UI always reflects the current application state.

---

# Core Principles

## 1. Single Source of Truth

Every piece of information should have one authoritative owner.

Examples

Career Content

↓

Database

User Progress

↓

Database

Current UI State

↓

Local State

Authentication

↓

Auth Provider

Never duplicate state.

---

## 2. Server First

Persistent data belongs on the server.

Examples

Progress

Notes

Bookmarks

Portfolio

Projects

Quiz Results

Certificates

Profile

Never rely on client memory for important data.

---

## 3. Local State Only for UI

Local state should only manage temporary interface behavior.

Examples

Modal open

Accordion expanded

Selected tab

Search input

Hovered card

Loading spinner

Never store business data only in local state.

---

## 4. Optimistic Updates

User actions should feel instant.

Flow

User Action

↓

Optimistic UI Update

↓

Server Update

↓

Confirmation

↓

Rollback if failed

---

# State Categories

The application contains four categories of state.

---

# 1. Global Application State

Available everywhere.

Contains

Current User

Authentication

Theme

Language

Notifications

Search

Current Career

Current Workspace

Feature Flags

Network Status

---

# 2. User State

Contains

Profile

Experience

Target Career

Bookmarks

Achievements

Learning Preferences

Completed Careers

Learning Streak

Career Readiness

---

# 3. Career State

Scoped to one career.

Contains

Roadmap

Skills

Projects

Certificates

Resources

Progress

Notes

Quiz Results

Portfolio

---

# 4. UI State

Temporary interface state.

Contains

Modal

Drawer

Expanded Accordion

Selected Tab

Sorting

Filtering

Pagination

Search Query

---

# Data Ownership

Each entity has one owner.

Career

Database

Course

Database

Project

Database

User Progress

Database

Theme

Global App State

Current Modal

Local Component

Search Text

Search Component

Accordion

Component

---

# State Persistence

Persist automatically

Progress

Bookmarks

Portfolio

Notes

Completed Courses

Quiz Results

Certificates

Projects

Resume

Settings

Do NOT persist

Hover state

Dropdown open

Tooltip

Loading spinner

Temporary filters

